{"reference":"Amos 3","book":"Amos","chapter":3,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A Chosen People and Accountability","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Amos 3:1-2 presents Israel’s being “known” by Jehovah, after being brought from Egypt, as the basis for accountability rather than protection from judgment. On this reading, election is neither a claim of ethnic superiority nor something erased by Israel’s wrongdoing; it makes the announced reckoning for iniquities more pointed.","verse_refs":["Amos 3:1-15"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_amos_003_01d10d96d1cf18d75dca677d"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}